
#DESCRIPTION
2D oblique shock with the hybrid solver at dx = 0.5 d_i over about three ion
gyroperiods: flow along x into a reflecting left wall, open inflow right
boundary, upstream field at 45 deg to the shock normal. Grid-scale noise is
damped by the upwind (Rusanov) dissipation of the Ohm's-law E with the MC
limiter and the flow plus fast-wave signal speed; without any dissipation the
|B| overshoot grows to about 3 and grid-scale noise to about 18 % of the field
power.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
0.0                     xMin
64.0                    xMax
-4.0                    yMin
 4.0                    yMax
-0.5                    zMin
 0.5                    zMax

#NCELL
128                     nCellX
16                      nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
16                      maxBlockSizeX
16                      maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
F                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#FIELDBOXBOUNDARY
outflow                 fieldBoxBoundaryLo
fixed                   fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi

#PARTICLEBOXBOUNDARY
reflect                 particleBoxBoundaryLo
inflow                  particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#HALLTERM
T                       useHallTerm

#FIELDSUBCYCLE
4                       nSubcycle
F                       isAutoSubcycle

#HYBRIDUPWIND
T                       useHybridUpwind
mc                      upwindLimiter
0.0                     upwindCoefWhistler

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
141.0                   electronTemperature
1.6667                  electronGamma
5.0                     electronDensity0

#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#INFLOW
5.0                     rho [/cc]
-713.0                  ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
6.28e5                  T [K]

motional E = -u x B = (0, ux*Bz, 0); ux=-713e3 m/s, Bz=7.382e-9 T
   -> Ey = ux*Bz = -5.263e-3 V/m
#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho
-713.0                  ux
0.0                     uy
0.0                     uz
6.28e5                  T
7.382e-9                bx
0.0                     by
7.382e-9                bz
0.0                     ex
-5.263e-3               ey
0.0                     ez

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.005                   dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI
1.0e5                   uNormSI

#MONITOR
200                     dnReport
400                     dnReportLB
T                       doCompact

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
10                      npcelx
10                      npcely
1                       npcelz

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
5.0                     dt
1                       dx

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
20.0                    TimeMax
